### Taxi_Server — API smoke tests
### Run the API first:  dotnet run --project src/Taxi.Api
### Ports come from src/Taxi.Api/Properties/launchSettings.json

@baseUrl = https://localhost:7007
@lang = en

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Authenticate — seeded Manager account
### Copy `accessToken` from the response into @token below.
# @name generateToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/token/generate
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

{
  "email": "admin@taxi.com",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### Set from the response above
@token = {{generateToken.response.body.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{generateToken.response.body.refreshToken}}

### 1a. Bad password → 401, message localized by Accept-Language.
### Unknown email and locked-out account (5 failures → 15 min) answer exactly the same.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/token/generate
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: ar

{
  "email": "admin@taxi.com",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 1a-2. Read-only account (role `User`) — can list cars, gets 403 on writes
# @name generateUserToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/token/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@taxi.com",
  "password": "User123!"
}

@userToken = {{generateUserToken.response.body.accessToken}}

### 1b. Refresh the access token (rotates the refresh token — one live token per user)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/token/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expiredAccessToken": "{{token}}",
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### 1c. Current user info (cached under CacheTags.UserInfo)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/token/user-info
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1d. Account self-service (all on the strict Auth rate limit)
### With Email:Provider=Log the emails (and their links) are written to the API console;
### under docker compose they land in Mailpit: http://localhost:8025

### Register → 202 (also 202 if the email already exists — no enumeration)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

{
  "email": "rider@taxi.com",
  "password": "Rider123!"
}

### Confirm — paste userId and token from the emailed link → 204
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/confirm-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "<userId from the link>",
  "token": "<token from the link>"
}

### Forgot password → 202 (only confirmed accounts get an email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: ar

{
  "email": "rider@taxi.com"
}

### Reset password with the emailed token → 204, revokes every refresh token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "rider@taxi.com",
  "token": "<token from the link>",
  "newPassword": "Rider456!"
}

### Change own password → 204 (wrong current password → 400 keyed "CurrentPassword")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "Admin123!",
  "newPassword": "Admin123!"
}

### Logout → 204: the refresh token is revoked; the access token lives until it expires
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Manager only: replace a user's roles → 204 (own Manager role cannot be removed → 409)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/<userId>/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roles": ["User"]
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Cars — the reference feature

### 2a. List cars, paged (cached per page: GetCarsQuery, tag "car", 10 min, culture-aware)
### Response: { items, page, pageSize, totalCount, totalPages, hasPreviousPage, hasNextPage }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

### 2a-2. Filter and sort: make or model contains "cam", newest model year first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars?search=cam&sortBy=year&sortDirection=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

### 2a-3. Exact make and year
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars?make=tesla&year=2024
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2a-4. API v2: the description in both languages + timestamps (v1 answers with a Sunset header)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/cars?pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2b. Same list in Arabic — separate cache entry (`cars_ar`), different description
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept-Language: ar

### 2c. Create a car → 201 + Location: /api/v1/cars/{guid}
# @name createCar
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

{
  "make": "Toyota",
  "model": "Camry",
  "year": 2024,
  "descriptionEn": "A reliable mid-size sedan.",
  "descriptionAr": "سيارة سيدان متوسطة الحجم وموثوقة."
}

@carId = {{createCar.response.body.id}}

### 2c-2. Idempotent create: run twice — one car, the second answer has Idempotency-Replayed: true.
### Same key with a different body → 422; while the first is still running → 409.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 6f1c2d4e-demo-key-0001

{
  "make": "Volkswagen",
  "model": "Golf",
  "year": 2023,
  "descriptionEn": "Created once, however often you retry.",
  "descriptionAr": "تُنشأ مرة واحدة مهما أعدت المحاولة."
}

### 2c-3. Upload the car image (multipart, field "file": JPEG/PNG/WebP, ≤ 5 MB) → 204
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/{{carId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=CarImage

--CarImage
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="car.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./car.png
--CarImage--

### 2c-4. Download it (404 if the car has none)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/{{carId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2d. Get one car (cached: GetCarByIdQuery). Run twice — the second hit should not query the DB.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/{{carId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

### 2e. Update → 204, and evicts the "car" cache tag
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/{{carId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "make": "Toyota",
  "model": "Camry Hybrid",
  "year": 2025,
  "descriptionEn": "A reliable mid-size hybrid sedan.",
  "descriptionAr": "سيارة سيدان هجينة متوسطة الحجم وموثوقة."
}

### 2f. Re-list — the update must be visible (proves tag invalidation)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

### 2g. Delete → 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/{{carId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2x. Drivers — second reference: child collection, relationship, domain event

### Create → 201 (licence numbers are unique, case-insensitive)
# @name createDriver
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/drivers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Sami Haddad",
  "licenseNumber": "DL-{{$randomInt 1000 9999}}"
}

@driverId = {{createDriver.response.body.id}}

### Add a certification (child collection; name in both languages, future expiry) → 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/drivers/{{driverId}}/certifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nameEn": "First aid",
  "nameAr": "الإسعافات الأولية",
  "expiresOn": "2030-01-01"
}

### Assign a car (one driver per car) → 204; raises DriverAssignedToCarDomainEvent via the outbox
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/drivers/{{driverId}}/car
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "carId": "{{carId}}"
}

### Deleting an assigned car → 409 "The car is assigned to a driver"
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/{{carId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read it back — certification names follow Accept-Language
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/drivers/{{driverId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept-Language: ar

### Unassign → 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/drivers/{{driverId}}/car
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List, searching name or licence
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/drivers?search=sami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Failure paths

### 3a. No token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars

### 3a-2. Authenticated but not a Manager → 403 (policy CanManageCars)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "make": "Fiat",
  "model": "Panda",
  "year": 2020,
  "descriptionEn": "Readers cannot write.",
  "descriptionAr": "القراء لا يكتبون."
}

### 3b. Unknown id → 404, title from LocalizationKeys.Car.NotFound
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3b-2. Invalid page → 400 keyed by "Page" (pageSize above 100 is clamped, not rejected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars?page=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

### 3b-3. Unknown sort field → 400 keyed by "SortBy" (whitelist: make, model, year, createdAt)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars?sortBy=price
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

### 3c. Invalid year → 400 ValidationProblemDetails keyed by "Year"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: {{lang}}

{
  "make": "Ford",
  "model": "Model T",
  "year": 1500,
  "descriptionEn": "Too old to be valid.",
  "descriptionAr": "قديمة جدًا."
}

### 3d. Same, in Arabic — the validation message must be translated
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: ar

{
  "make": "Ford",
  "model": "Model T",
  "year": 1500,
  "descriptionEn": "Too old to be valid.",
  "descriptionAr": "قديمة جدًا."
}

### 3e. Update an unknown id → 404 (the id comes from the route only; the body has none)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "make": "Toyota",
  "model": "Camry",
  "year": 2024,
  "descriptionEn": "Nobody home.",
  "descriptionAr": "لا أحد هنا."
}

